{"step_index":52,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:39:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-23T13:39:48+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-23T13:39:48+07:00\nShowing lines 1-63 of 63\n1: ## Standards\n2: \n3: *Reviewed against Rust best practices, Clippy idioms, and Fowler baseline smells in [`src/core/srt.rs`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs).*\n4: \n5: ### Hard Violations\n6: 1. **`clippy::format_push_string` in [`serialize_srt`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L117-L120)**\n7:    - **Rule**: Avoid `string.push_str(&format!(...))` in loops; it causes redundant intermediate heap allocations per iteration.\n8:    - **Remedy**: Import `std::fmt::Write` and format directly via `write!(output, \"...\\n\", ...)`.\n9: 2. **Inconsistent Qualification / Unused Import in [`src/core/srt.rs`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L3-L16)**\n10:    - **Rule**: Avoid redundant path qualification when the type is already imported.\n11:    - **Hunk**: `use std::path::PathBuf;` is imported at line 3, but `SubtitleFile` declares `pub path: Option<std::path::PathBuf>`.\n12:    - **Remedy**: Use `pub path: Option<PathBuf>`.\n13: 3. **Eager Full-Buffer Allocation in [`parse_srt`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L37-L40)**\n14:    - **Rule**: Prefer zero-copy parsing over full-file string reallocations.\n15:    - **Hunk**: `clean_text = content...replace(\"\\r\\n\", \"\\n\")` allocates a full copy of the entire file buffer solely to normalize line breaks.\n16:    - **Remedy**: Iterate with `str::lines()` or strip trailing `\\r` per line without reallocating the input buffer.\n17: \n18: ### Judgement Calls & Code Smells\n19: 1. **Primitive Obsession ([`SubtitleLine`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L8-L9))**\n20:    - **Issue**: SRT timestamps (`00:00:01,000`) are stored and returned (`parse_timestamps -> Option<(String, String)>`) as raw `String`s without validation, comparison, or offset calculation capability. A dedicated `Timestamp` or duration type provides type safety.\n21: 2. **Feature Envy ([`serialize_srt`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L101))**\n22:    - **Issue**: Standalone function reaches deeply into the internal fields of both `SubtitleFile` and `SubtitleLine`.\n23:    - **Remedy**: Implement this as an inherent method (`SubtitleFile::to_srt(&self, use_translated: bool)`) or implement `std::fmt::Display` on `SubtitleLine`.\n24: 3. **Redundant Intermediate Collections ([`parse_srt`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L45-L49))**\n25:    - **Issue**: Materializing intermediate `Vec<&str>` buffers (`clean_text.split(\"\\n\\n\").collect()` and `block_lines.collect()`) where iterator pipelines suffice.\n26: 4. **Dropped Error Context in [`parse_srt`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L63-L64)**\n27:    - **Rule**: Standard library error wrapping should preserve underlying cause.\n28:    - **Issue**: `index_str.parse::<usize>().map_err(...)` discards the underlying `ParseIntError`. Prefer preserving the source error in `SrtError`.\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## Spec\n33: \n34: *Reviewed against [CONTEXT.md](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/CONTEXT.md#L21-L28) (Subtitle & Document Domain).*\n35: \n36: ### (a) Missing or Partial Requirements\n37: 1. **Line Status Lifecycle**\n38:    - **Spec Quote**: `Line Status: The lifecycle state of a line during translation ('Pending', 'Translating', 'Done', 'Error').`\n39:    - **Finding**: Completely missing. `SubtitleLine` does not include a `status` field, and no `LineStatus` enum is defined.\n40: 2. **Duration & CPS Calculations**\n41:    - **Spec Quote**: `Duration ($T_{\\text{duration}}$): The active on-screen display duration of a subtitle line, calculated as $T_{\\text{end}} - T_{\\text{start}}$ in seconds.`\n42:    - **Spec Quote**: `Characters Per Second (CPS): The reading speed density metric calculated as $\\frac{\\text{Length of Text}}{T_{\\text{duration}}}$.`\n43:    - **Finding**: Missing. `SubtitleLine` stores timestamps as unvalidated strings with no methods to calculate active on-screen duration or reading speed density.\n44: 3. **Duration Alert Logic**\n45:    - **Spec Quote**: `Duration Alert: A warning triggered when $T_{\\text{duration}} < 1.0\\text{s}$ or $\\text{CPS} > 20$...`\n46:    - **Finding**: Domain calculation / threshold check for duration and CPS alerts is not implemented.\n47: \n48: ### (b) Scope Creep (Unrequested Behaviour)\n49: 1. **SRT Serialization with Translation Fallback ([`serialize_srt`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L101-L124))**\n50:    - **Spec Quote**: `- **SubtitleFile**: An in-memory document model representing a parsed subtitle file with an optional file path and a list of SubtitleLine items.`\n51:    - **Finding**: The spec defines document models and domain rules; `serialize_srt` with translation fallback logic was not requested as part of the initial parsing/domain model specification.\n52: \n53: ### (c) Requirements Implemented Incorrectly\n54: 1. **Timestamp Format Validation**\n55:    - **Spec Quote**: `start timestamp string ('00:00:01,000'), end timestamp string ('00:00:04,000')`\n56:    - **Finding**: [`parse_timestamps`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L87-L100) only splits by `-->` and checks non-empty slices. Non-standard timestamp strings (e.g. `\"foo --> bar\"`) pass parsing without validating the SRT timecode structure (`HH:MM:SS,mmm`).\n57: 2. **File Path Handling**\n58:    - **Spec Quote**: `SubtitleFile: An in-memory document model representing a parsed subtitle file with an optional file path and a list of SubtitleLine items.`\n59:    - **Finding**: [`parse_srt`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/srt.rs#L85) hardcodes `path: None` without an API to retain or associate the file path when loading from disk.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: **Summary**: Standards: 7 findings (worst: unnecessary full-buffer reallocation and loop `format_push_string` heap allocations); Spec: 6 findings (worst: missing `LineStatus` model and missing $T_{\\text{duration}}$ / CPS calculation logic)."}
{"step_index":53,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:39:48Z","input_tokens":2063,"cache_read_tokens":51770,"output_tokens":1101,"thinking":"Observing the file `.scratch/subtitle-ai-translation/code-reveiew.md`, the structure for file reviews in this repository is clear. Need to initiate the parallel research sub-agents mandated by the `/code-review` skill. One sub-agent will focus on standards.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Model":"inherit","Prompt":"Review `/home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs` (untracked/new file on `feat/core-ai` compared to `main`) for the **Standards** axis.\n\nStandards sources in the repo:\n- `/home/derek/projects/ryz/CONTEXT.md`\n- `/home/derek/projects/ryz/docs/adr/0002-decoupled-generic-ai-client.md`\n- Standard Rust / Clippy idioms\n\nPlus the Fowler smell baseline:\n- **Mysterious Name**: a function, variable, or type whose name doesn't reveal what it does or holds. → rename it; if no honest name comes, the design's murky.\n- **Duplicated Code**: the same logic shape appears in more than one hunk or file in the change. → extract the shared shape, call it from both.\n- **Feature Envy**: a method that reaches into another object's data more than its own. → move the method onto the data it envies.\n- **Data Clumps**: the same few fields or params keep travelling together (a type wanting to be born). → bundle them into one type, pass that.\n- **Primitive Obsession**: a primitive or string standing in for a domain concept that deserves its own type. → give the concept its own small type.\n- **Repeated Switches**: the same `switch`/`if`-cascade on the same type recurs across the change. → replace with polymorphism, or one map both sites share.\n- **Shotgun Surgery**: one logical change forces scattered edits across many files in the diff. → gather what changes together into one module.\n- **Divergent Change**: one file or module is edited for several unrelated reasons. → split so each module changes for one reason.\n- **Speculative Generality**: abstraction, parameters, or hooks added for needs the spec doesn't have. → delete it; inline back until a real need shows.\n- **Message Chains**: long `a.b().c().d()` navigation the caller shouldn't depend on. → hide the walk behind one method on the first object.\n- **Middle Man**: a class or function that mostly just delegates onward. → cut it, call the real target direct.\n- **Refused Bequest**: a subclass or implementer that ignores or overrides most of what it inherits. → drop the inheritance, use composition.\n\nBrief:\nReport, per file/hunk where relevant, (a) every place the code in `/home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs` violates a documented standard or Rust idiom: cite the standard/rule; and (b) any baseline smell you spot: name it and quote the hunk. Distinguish hard violations from judgement calls: documented-standard breaches can be hard, but baseline smells are always judgement calls, and a documented repo standard overrides the baseline. Skip anything tooling enforces. Under 400 words. Use clickable markdown file links `[ai.rs](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L...)`.","Role":"Standards Code Reviewer","TypeName":"research"}},{"name":"invoke_subagent","args":{"Model":"inherit","Prompt":"Review `/home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs` for the **Spec** axis against:\n- `/home/derek/projects/ryz/.scratch/subtitle-ai-translation/issues/02-headless-ai-client.md`\n- `/home/derek/projects/ryz/.scratch/subtitle-ai-translation/spec.md`\n- `/home/derek/projects/ryz/docs/adr/0002-decoupled-generic-ai-client.md`\n- `/home/derek/projects/ryz/CONTEXT.md`\n\nBrief:\nReport: (a) requirements the spec asked for that are missing or partial; (b) behaviour in the file that wasn't asked for (scope creep); (c) requirements that look implemented but where the implementation looks wrong (including unused `system` and `user` parameters in `text(system: &str, user: &str)`). Quote the spec line for each finding. Under 400 words. Use clickable markdown file links `[ai.rs](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L...)`.","Role":"Spec Code Reviewer","TypeName":"research"}}]}
